==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Ultimate Lasvoss''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Lasvoss Reborn''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Lasvoss' unparalleled attack force at medium range is his main driving factor when it comes to his usage. At level 30, a strengthened Lasvoss can deal almost 460k damage with his Savage Blow; however, not only is this monstrous power fueled by chance, but Lasvoss' low survivability and range makes him impractical to use in most circumstances as he will frequently get hit and die without doing much, greatly weakening his capability as a generalist while still wasting your resources.

Lasvoss can counter a decent amount of enemies thanks to his immunity to [[Wave Attack]]s and almost all debuffs, including [[Kory]], [[Berserkory]], [[Dober P.D]] and even [[Hermit Cat (Enemy)|Hermit Cat]], as he can stand away from their line of fire and still deal heavy damage when supported properly. Besides those few instances, Lasvoss can be considered a [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] that trades range for overall damage.

Lasvoss is also in one of the best "Research" Effect UP [[Cat Combo|Combos]] in the game, [[Bad Guys (Combo)|Bad Guys]], which helps for cats whose recharge times are just shy of being meatshield-caliber, such as [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Rocker Cat]] or [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Mer-Cat]] and even [[Killer Cat (Rare Cat)|Radical Cat]] though with the down side of being 3 slots. This in turn makes it so that Cheating Heart has a slightly lower effect but is able to be just 2 slots. Cheating Heart also already lowers the recharge time to almost 2 seconds anyway for cats that use them such as the mentioned Rocker Cat and Mer-Cat though you also get to use Lasvoss alongside them so that could be a turning point of this combo.

Lasvoss' main niche is to perform a single hit on a threatening enemy, either completely eliminating it, or doing a considerable chunk into its health. As a midranger, Lasvoss doesn't have much survivability, and should not be expected to land multiple hits due to its long attack cycle.

==='''True Form'''===
Lasvoss' True Form is a significant upgrade, doubling his HP and increasing his base damage by 50%, as well as giving him more immunities. While his Strengthen now triggers at 30% HP instead of 1% HP, he still cannot reliably make use of it as it is not tied to a knockback, and the only knockback that happens after this Strengthen starts is when he survives a lethal strike. His new immunities are the most important improvements, granting him immunity to '''[[Toxic]]''' and '''[[Surge Attack]]s'''. Both effects are notoriously rare to find counters to, granting him a niche against many dangerous enemies including but not limited to: [[St. Dober]], the [[Surge Base (Enemy Base)|Surge Base]], [[Gobble]], [[Zollow]], [[Master Uril (Enemy)|Master Uril]], [[Kappy Jr.]] and [[:Category:Death Surge Enemies|Death Surge enemies]]. However, these benefits come with a ''steep'' [[Catfruit]] cost, requiring ten Epic Seeds, one Elder Catfruit and one Gold Catfruit, making this form a high cost, high reward one. If you are in late game then it is highly recommended to evolve Lasvoss, consider the fact that in late game, most of the enemies are going to be so buffed that you might just need some nuking power. But make sure you use him correctly to redeem his cost.

==='''Talents'''===
With Talents, Lasvoss Reborn gains the usual HP/Attack buffs, but also Colossus Slayer, Move Speed Up and Recover Speed Up. The standard stat talents are great for Lasvoss as he makes use of every bit of it, HP buff allowing him to land hits more consistently and get more out of strengthen, while Attack Up pushes his already insane damage even higher. '''Colossus Slayer''' is quite notable, giving an otherwise unspecialized unit a niche to work with. As a midranger, Lasvoss is unable to fight most [[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]] threats directly despite his relatively low recharge time for an Uber, as Colossus enemies often boast extreme stats with high range and sometimes [[Omni Strike]], so unless he gets the range advantage, he cannot reliably deal high damage and more often than not relies on timing in order to leave any impact, not to mention he remains a huge resource drain. If he does land a hit, though, he can still do high amount of damage on them. '''Move Speed Up''' makes it far easier for Lasvoss to approach enemies, especially if they outrange him. It also brings him to the frontline much faster which can help with timing. Although this upgrade may slightly reduce Lasvoss' survivability, the benefits he gains are easily worth it. '''Recover Speed Up''' is nearly useless. Although Lasvoss has a much faster recharge compared to other Uber Rares, this upgrade does not do enough to make him spammable, and his cost is too high for frequent deployment regardless.

