==Trivia==
*While Lasvoss's name is a corruption of "last boss", it also sounds similar to [[wikia:chrono:Lavos|Lavos]], the final boss of ''[[wikipedia:Chrono Trigger|Chrono Trigger]]''.
**He also shares some similarities to Lavos in his design, suggesting that it was one of, if not the main inspiration.
*Lasvoss' designs are based on common features of final bosses in RPGs: his Normal Form resembles "floating head and hands" bosses such as the [https://dragon-quest.org/wiki/File:DQT_Archfiend_Mortamor.png final form] of [https://dragon-quest.org/wiki/Mortamor Mortamor] from ''[[wikipedia:Dragon Quest|Dragon Quest]]'', while Ultimate Lasvoss resembles ''[[wikipedia:Final Fantasy V|Final Fantasy V]]''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s final boss, Neo Exdeath. His Strengthen ability represents how final bosses often attain a more powerful form after losing enough health.
*In the event poster for [[THE DYNAMITES (Gacha Event)|THE DYNAMITES]], Lasvoss is accompanied by the phrase, "My servant, I grant thee rule over 1/3 of this world!" This is a reference to part of a quote from the main antagonist of the original ''Dragon Quest'', the [https://dragon-quest.org/wiki/Dragonlord Dragonlord]: "Take thy rightful place at my side! Do so, and I will grant unto thee dominion over half the world!"
*Like pre-talents [[Nobiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Nobilan Pasalan]] and [[Li'l Valkyrie (Uber Rare Cat)|Li'l Valkyrie]], Lasvoss' Curse Immunity is useless due to his lack of any anti-trait abilities.
*Lasvoss Reborn is the only [[True Form]] in the game to require more than one [[Catfruit|Epic Catfruit Seed]].
*The heroes referenced in his descriptions are likely [[Cat Clan Heroes (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Clan Heroes]].
*Lasvoss currently boasts the single highest damaging attack of any cat unit in the game, especially with full investment.
**At level 60+70, with max [[Talents]], against a [[Colossus Enemies|Colossus]] enemy, holding an S-rank Uncanny Legends [[Talent Orbs|Talent Orb]], using [[Cosplay Fans (Combo)|Cosplay Fans]] and [[Land-Air Assault (Combo)|Land-Air Assault]] (+30% Strengthen Effect UP & 15% Unit Attack UP), with a [[Savage Blow]] while [[Strengthen|Strengthened]], Lasvoss is able to dish out '''6,574,892 damage''' in a single hit.

